    "### 11. Gradient of Log-Determinant\n",
    "Using Jacobi's formula, the differential of determinant is $d \\det(X) = \\det(X) \\text{tr}(X^{-1} dX)$.\n",
    "Hence,\n",
    "$$d \\log \\det(X) = \\frac{d \\det(X)}{\\det(X)} = \\text{tr}(X^{-1} dX)$$\n",
    "Since $df = \\text{tr}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial X}\\right)^T dX\\right)$, we have:\n",
    "$$\\left(\\frac{\\partial \\log \\det(X)}{\\partial X}\\right)^T = X^{-1} \\implies \\frac{\\partial \\log \\det(X)}{\\partial X} = X^{-T}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = np.random.randn(3, 3)\n",
    "X = X @ X.T  # make positive definite\n",
    "grad_analytical = np.linalg.inv(X).T\n",
    "print(\"Log-det gradient (analytical):\\n\", grad_analytical)"
   ]
  },
